# File: tests/blender/test_variants_clean.py
# Generated from: specs/140-fix-finalize-export-failing-the-contract-on-mobile-lods-the-variants-step-decimated/requirements.md
Feature: Variants step produces Mobile meshes that pass the contract

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Decimated LODs have no degenerate or loose geometry
    Given a rigged asset whose Desktop mesh is above the Mobile budget and whose decimation produces a zero-area face
    When the variants step builds "<Name>_Mobile"
    Then contract validation reports no "geometry.zero_area" and no "geometry.loose" finding on any Mobile LOD

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Decimated LODs have stable normals
    Given a Desktop mesh containing a tiny face on a non-manifold edge
    When cleanup_desktop and then the variants step run
    Then contract validation reports no "geometry.normals" finding on the Desktop mesh or on any Mobile LOD
    And repeating the validation gives the same result

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: The Mobile root is re-seated after decimation
    Given an asset where decimation removes a bounding-box extreme vertex
    When the variants step builds "<Name>_Mobile"
    Then the Mobile variant's origin and bounding-box bottom centre are within the contract pivot tolerance of the world origin
    And no "pivot.bottom_center" finding is reported

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Desktop cleanup removes non-manifold-edge faces and duplicate faces
    Given a Desktop mesh with a face on a non-manifold edge and two faces that share an identical vertex set
    When cleanup_desktop runs
    Then the offending non-manifold face is removed
    And one face remains for the shared vertex set
    And the reported "tris_after" reflects the removals

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Re-import triangle counts match
    Given the asset with a non-manifold-edge face and duplicate faces taken through variants, export, and reimport
    When the reimport check compares each FBX with its report
    Then no "reimport.tris" finding is reported for the Desktop or any Mobile mesh

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Budgets, skinning, and layout are preserved
    Given rigged, unrigged single-mesh, and multi-part assets
    When the variants step runs with the post-decimation clean
    Then every LOD stays within its triangle target
    And rigged LODs keep their Armature modifier and vertex groups
    And the LOD layout is unchanged
    And the "lod_tris" in the step result equal the cleaned meshes' counts

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Clean meshes are unchanged
    Given an asset whose Desktop mesh and decimated LODs already satisfy the contract
    When cleanup_desktop and the variants step run
    Then triangle counts and pivots match the previous behavior
    And identical input yields identical output
